{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_cumulants_not_derived_pattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_cumulants_not_derived_pattern","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L169-L174","doc":"The forward cumulants are NOT the derived residual cumulants: their sign\npattern is `(−,+)`, not the derived `(+,−)`.  Recorded as a single conjunction for\ndownstream citation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_ratio_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_ratio_two","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L163-L167","doc":"**Honest NEGATIVE — wrong magnitude ratio.**  The forward 4-body/3-body\nmagnitude ratio is exactly `2` (`ν₄ = −2·ν₃`), whereas the derived residual needs\n`|μ₄/μ₃| ≈ 9.75`.  The ≥3-row combinatorial content does not supply the derived\nmagnitude ratio (miss ≈ 4.9×). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_sign_window_opposite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_sign_window_opposite","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L155-L161","doc":"**Honest NEGATIVE — wrong sign-change order.**  The forward ≥3-row cumulants\nsatisfy `ν₃ < 0 ∧ 0 < ν₄`, i.e. the `(−,+)` order.  The derived residual cumulants\nare `(μ₃, μ₄) = (+, −)` (the #4316 sign window `κ ∈ (3/2,3)`).  So the proved `Δ_λ`\nchirality parity produces the **opposite** 3-body/4-body sign change; it does not\nsupply the many-body binding sign-change window.  Scope-(a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_edge_coeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.forward_edge_coeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L149-L153","doc":"**0-fit structural match.**  The forward edge cumulant vanishes, `ν₂ = 0`,\nmatching the derived `μ₂ = 0` of `AdditiveResidualSimplex` — but derived here\ncombinatorially (`s₁ = s₂ = 0`), q₀-free and independent of the graded-ladder\ndeuteron self-reference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu_values","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L146-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu4","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L143-L144","doc":"Forward 4-body (tetrahedron) cumulant `ν₄ = S(4) − 6·ν₂ − 4·ν₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu3","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L141-L142","doc":"Forward 3-body (triangle) cumulant `ν₃ = S(3) − 3·ν₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.nu2","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L139-L140","doc":"Forward 2-body (edge) cumulant `ν₂ = S(2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Salg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Salg","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L136-L137","doc":"Single-algebra reading: `S(A) = s_A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_deuteron_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_deuteron_zero","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L129-L132","doc":"The deuteron extensive value is `0`: consistent with the general\n`clusterF_eq_zero_of_card_le_two`.  The deuteron binding is a separate 2-body\nobject, not a ≥3-body cluster term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_ratio_four_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_ratio_four_three","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L121-L127","doc":"**The extensive `A=4 / A=3` ratio identity is exactly `6`** (⁴He / ³H skeleton):\n`Bext 4 = 6 · Bext 3`.  Contrast the AME ratio `B(⁴He)/B(³H) ≈ 3.336` (probe): the\nextensive reading overshoots by `+80 %`, 0-fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_four","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L118-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_three","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L116-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext_two","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L114-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.Bext","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L110-L112","doc":"The homogeneous evaluation of the extensive cluster functional at `A` nucleons:\n`Bext A = Σ_k C(A,k)·s_k` (terms with `k < 3` vanish since `s_k = 0` there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.clusterF_eq_zero_of_card_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.clusterF_eq_zero_of_card_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L96-L106","doc":"**Irreducibly ≥3-body.**  On any set of `≤ 2` nucleons the cluster functional\nvanishes identically, for *any* weight `w` — no `≥3`-element subset exists.  This is\nthe deuteron structural fact: `A = 2` carries no many-body cluster term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.clusterF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.clusterF","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L89-L94","doc":"The extensive (size-consistent) cluster functional over a nucleon set `S`,\nbuilt from a per-cardinality weight `w` supported on cardinalities `≥ 3`: it sums\n`w |T|` over every subset `T ⊆ S` with `|T| ≥ 3`.  Additive over disjoint subsets\nby construction; irreducibly ≥3-body because subsets of size `< 3` contribute `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.sRow3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.sRow3","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ThreeRowExtensiveCumulant.lean#L77-L85","doc":"`s_k = Σ_{λ⊢k, ℓ(λ)≥3} (−1)^{n(λ)}·f^λ`, the Δ_λ of\n`dtEuler_eq_deltaLambda_unconditional` restricted to the ≥3-row stratum.  Concrete\ninteger values at `k ≤ 5` (Python-verified in the companion probe); `0` for\n`k ≤ 2` because no partition of `k ≤ 2` has `≥ 3` rows. ","signatureChunk":0}]}